 avoid as well so I do take  some long walks and I've done that over  the course of the year but I also did  get back to the gym and started doing  weight circuit training you know  sometimes less regularly sometimes more  covid really put a big  Kink into that because I I did suffer  some effects you know lasting past the  initial infection  making me a bit more tired when I would  exercise and you know things things  along those lines  but you know overall it's been pretty  good I've I've over the last year I've  lost about 30 pounds and it's not  actually like losing 30 pounds  completely because what I what ended up  happening is a net loss of 30 pounds  which means a lot of fat got lost or  burned off rather and then I added some  muscle which is good as well and the  muscle is good for keeping the fat off  right because muscle demands more energy  to to keep itself going it's kind of a  virtuous cycle and you know getting back  into the gym there have been some ups  and downs you know so some of it  involves some mental adjustment you know  there's there's like you get to a  certain level with the weights you've  been making some gains and then you know  you can't go for a while then you got to  start out at a lower level well that  takes some mental Readjustment which is  which is is good for me as well  what else you know it's it's been quite  an active year as far as tutorials I  picked up a number of new clients and  um you know doing philosophical  counseling with some clients uh some  academic coaching here and there  got brought in on you know quite a few  uh projects uh here and there as well so  so that's that's good and you know I  this might actually be the year that I  start getting my act together as far as  marketing goes I'm very fortunate in  that so far everybody's sought me out I  haven't like advertised or marketed or  anything like that and I've had a pretty  steady flow of clients coming to me to  work on interesting and challenging  matters using the resources of  philosophy  um what else so you know I'm a team  member of the modern stoicism  organization and you know I I helped  along with my my wife and a few other  people to organize the annual stoicon  conference which went quite well we we  actually had almost no problems uh in  the course of the the conference which  is almost unheard of for something  that's online so you know everybody  showed up where they're supposed to we  didn't have any terrible tiffs or  technology failures or anything like  that so that was that was really awesome  we raised a good bit of money for the  modern stoicism organization  um Leia goldrick and I also managed to  bring out the uh fourth volume in  stoicism today selected essays we'd  brought out volume three in 2021 and we  brought out volume four this year so  that's really cool you know another  edited volume uh the proceeds of which  go to the modern stoicism organize  so that was really quite quite awesome  and lovely and then  what else oh I stepped down as of the  end of the year as the editor of  stoicism today a role that I took out in  2016 so you know almost seven years had  passed and I thought it was time to you  know move on and bring on some fresh new  eyes and new blood so my assistant  editor and good friend and colleague  Harold coveley has moved up from  assistant Editor to to full editor and  Judith stove who is also you know a good  friend and very competent at what she  does and a great addition to the team  actually join the modern stoicism team  and came on as the assistant editor so  I'm happy leaving stoicism today in some  really competent hands and that'll give  me a bit more time to do some of the  work that that I want to do as as well  I got some writing work done  I've been working on taking the videos  that I did the commentary videos on  epictetuses and caridian taking the  transcripts from them cleaning them up  you know editing them and I'm turning  them slowly into a book form and I've  I've released them in serial form to my  patreon supporters and in medium and  eventually it's going to turn into  hopefully later on this year of 2023  into a new book that um will you know be  helpful for people in studying this  great short work of stoic philosophy  speaking of medium I managed to write 71  medium posts in the last year which is  you know pretty good not as not as much  as I'd like to but you know got some  writing done which is nice and I've you  know I've got my three different  Publications heavy metal philosopher  practical rationality and then Gregory  very Sadler PhD publishing in all of  those I might start publishing in 2023  and some other places as well but you  know we'll see what happens  um YouTube I think most of you probably  know me from YouTube and it's not a  surprise since you're watching this  right on YouTube right now  so it was a pretty good year  350 videos so not a video a day but  pretty close you know there's there's uh  some days that I I didn't release  anything  um  you know started some new things uh some  merch offering memberships  um started new video series like the  Sadler's quick takes and you know  um kept going on with like Sadler's  stories and book reviews and all of that  and I I did want to point out that  113 core concept videos I'm you know I  it's still nowhere near like full  coverage of even just the history of  Western philosophy but you know we're  filling in the gaps so doing the  medieval philosophy class was kind of  good because I didn't have that much in  that section so I did more videos on  Augustine and on uh Anselm who you know  I had videos on already but I got to  churn out a lot more and then there were  two other medieval authors who I hadn't  done  um prudentius this really Latin poet  early medieval I mean uh his cycle  machia and alquin who I've been a fan of  for quite a long time this great  Benedictine scholar associated with uh  Charlemagne and the carolaginian  Renaissance so I did one of his works as  well  and a bunch of others I mean I just  recently finished up a sequence on David  hume's inquiry concerning human  understanding  um you know all sorts of other cool  stuff along the way doing doing the  anger classes gave me an opportunity to  do some work on you know Aristotle and  Plutarch and Seneca and also you know  contemporary figures like audre Lorde uh  her work the uses of anger so lots and  lots of core concept videos  um it wasn't a great year for half hour  Hegel I did manage to get 23 new  commentary videos done and we're almost  at the very end of the religion section  of hegel's phenomenology so the end is  in sight we've just got one more video  to do in that and then we're into  absolute knowing  um what else uh you know world's a  speculative fiction we kept up the new  format I did nine sessions in that plus  one special interview  with the author of dare to know James  Kennedy which which was kind of cool to  do  um what else you know the wisdom for  Life radio show uh we're now making less  Headway that we used to be every two  weeks we'd put out a new episode this  year we did 13 episodes so really about  one a month but you know it's still uh  doing quite good uh you know I think  that this coming year will probably get  back to doing one every two weeks who  knows maybe we'll even step it up to new  episode every week so if you like you  know Community radio that you can listen  to online everywhere and you're into  philosophy you probably want to check  out the wisdom for Life show and what  else did we do  well you know the Sadler's lectures  podcast which I make from core concept  videos I managed to release  270 podcast episodes so you know  definitely not one a day but  you know that's quite a lot so that's  pretty cool you know we passed up the  800 episode Mark oh I should point out  too with YouTube  um I think that I passed the hundred  thousand subscriber Mark in 2021 but  they sent me t